'' See the source's header. A UDT reaching an RTL parameter declared FBSTRING* is
'' CONVERTED into a descriptor of its own, not passed as itself.
''
'' The assertion is on fb_WstrAssignToA -- the conversion fbc emits -- because the
'' call itself takes a pointer either way and reads right in both the broken and the
'' fixed IR. Without the conversion there is no such instruction at all.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/dylibload-udt-arg.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_WstrAssignToA
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_DylibLoad
